To follow-up on the NIMBLE users list, I was able to correspond with Mathieu off-list, and we identified a few minor issues in his model, which we were able to fix.  These issues amounted to borderline values being used as initial values, which gave log-probabilities of -Inf, and more subtly, numerical issues arising from inappropriate choices of initial values for several model parameters, leading to numerical underflow, and therefore probabilities identically equal to 0.  Mathieu and I were able to work through these problems, and get his model running.

On Fri, Nov 20, 2020 at 5:40 PM Daniel Turek <db...@williams.edu> wrote:
> Mathieu, thanks for emailing the users list.  I hope we can help resolve this quandary.  That said, speaking at least for myself, I don't think I can spot the issue without being able to reproduce the error myself.  I know you mentioned that sharing data publicly is not a good option, so maybe you could send it off list, or an alternative would be sharing a set of proxy data, which you could distribute, which also replicates the error.  Either way would work.
>
> Anyway, I hope we can figure it out, but being able to reproduce the error is paramount to the investigation.
>
> Cheers,
> Daniel
>
>
